// @run
// @log 14
// @log -1
// @log 30
// @log 7
// @log 99
// THE UN-ANNOTATED FACE (D1572). An un-annotated parameter's type is a hole, and a hole names
// no vocabulary, so the ARMS choose: all-integer-literal arms take the integer path and each
// arm defers a `==` constraint the CALL adjudicates — which is exactly what the hand-written
// if-chain twin (`if id == 0x10 { … }`) already did, so `match` costs the same annotation the
// twin does, namely none. This is the consumer's own VL-020 probe shape: it annotates nothing.
//
// A fixture that annotates every destination cannot see the missing-annotation defect, and
// this family had one: before the hole route the annotated spelling ran and this one refused
// with `match scrutinee must be a union or an integer, got _`.

function len(id) {
  match id {
    0x10 => 14
    _ => -1
  }
}

function span(id) {
  match id {
    0x12 | 0x13 => 30
    -1 => 99
    _ => 7
  }
}

print(len(0x10)) // 14
print(len(3)) // -1
print(span(0x13)) // 30
print(span(5)) // 7
print(span(-1)) // 99
